usage: opt.py [-h] [--seed SEED] [--nsamples NSAMPLES] [--percdamp PERCDAMP]
              [--sparsity SPARSITY] [--prunen PRUNEN] [--prunem PRUNEM]
              [--blocksize BLOCKSIZE] [--gmp] [--wbits WBITS]
              [--minlayer MINLAYER] [--maxlayer MAXLAYER]
              [--prune_only PRUNE_ONLY] [--invert] [--save SAVE] [--log_wandb]
              model {wikitext2,ptb,c4}

positional arguments:
  model                 OPT model to load; pass `facebook/opt-X`.
  {wikitext2,ptb,c4}    Where to extract calibration data from.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --seed SEED           Seed for sampling the calibration data.
  --nsamples NSAMPLES   Number of calibration data samples.
  --percdamp PERCDAMP   Percent of the average Hessian diagonal to use for
                        dampening.
  --sparsity SPARSITY   Target sparsity
  --prunen PRUNEN       N for N:M pruning.
  --prunem PRUNEM       M for N:M pruning.
  --blocksize BLOCKSIZE
                        Blocksize to use for adaptive mask selection.
  --gmp                 Whether to run the GMP baseline.
  --wbits WBITS         Whether to quantize as well.
  --minlayer MINLAYER   Prune all layers with id >= this.
  --maxlayer MAXLAYER   Prune all layers with id < this.
  --prune_only PRUNE_ONLY
                        Prune only layers that contain this text.
  --invert              Invert subset.
  --save SAVE           Path to saved model.
  --log_wandb           Whether to log to wandb.
